<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Nissho mulls S.African nickel plant - paper.</title>
<headline>Nissho mulls S.African nickel plant - paper.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Nissho Iwai Corp is planning a big investment in a non-ferrous metal refinery in South Africa, the Business Report newspaper said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Hitoshi Suzuki, the company's international planning and administration manager for Africa, told the paper in Tokyo that Nissho Iwai was most interested in a nickel refinery.</p>
<p>He gave no details of the location, cost or time-frame. &quot;It is too early for such details, but we are seriously considering such an investment,&quot; Suzuki said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
